#========================================
# -------- CAP_CMOMF EXTRACTION ---------
#========================================

# Reuses CapMomExtractor (rule_decks/custom_mom_extractor.lvs, symlinked from
# the sibling ihp-sg13g2): the extractor is generic, taking the device-class
# name by constructor and every layer from this hash. cap_cmomf therefore
# extracts into the same DeviceCustomMIM class, with the same mim_top /
# mim_btm terminals, as cap_cmim and cap_cmomi.
#
# Its two ports are sorted by x, so PLUS (left edge) becomes mim_top and
# MINUS (top edge) becomes mim_btm. w and l come from the marker bounding box:
# l is its width (X) and w its height (Y), which is why the PCell draws l along
# X. Both are non-primary parameters, so LVS compares this device
# topologically and never on its value.
#
# NOTE ON THE REGRESSION GROUP: this deck is named cap_cmomf_extraction.lvs, so
# run_regression.py classifies the device in group CAP_CMOMF and looks for its
# testcase under testcases/unit/cap_cmomf_devices/. The natural home is g2's
# shared cap_extraction.lvs (group CAP, alongside cap_cmomi), but that file is
# a symlink here and forking it to add one call is not worth the drift. When
# cap_cmomf is upstreamed the call folds in there and the testcase moves to
# cap_devices/.
logger.info('Extracting cap_cmomf device')
extract_devices(CapMomExtractor.new('cap_cmomf'), {
                  'core' => cap_cmomf_marker,
                  'm1p' => cap_cmomf_m1_ports,
                  'm2p' => cap_cmomf_m2_ports,
                  'm3p' => cap_cmomf_m3_ports,
                  'm4p' => cap_cmomf_m4_ports,
                  'm5p' => cap_cmomf_m5_ports,
                  'dev_mk' => cap_cmomf_dev_mk
                })
